#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
govc-safe - pseudonymising proxy for the govc CLI.

Runs govc with real credentials, then replaces every real identifier in the
output with a stable token before printing. The caller (an LLM agent) only ever
sees tokens: VM-0001, HOST-01, IP-0003.

Design notes:
  * Allowlist, not passthrough. Unknown verbs AND unknown flags are refused, so
    a future govc flag cannot silently become an exfiltration channel.
  * Learn-then-replace. Identifiers appear inside composite strings such as
    "[LocalDS_0] MyVM/MyVM.vmx", so walking JSON keys is not sufficient. We
    enumerate the inventory up front and substitute known names anywhere they
    occur, then sweep for IP/IPv6/MAC/UUID/email/user patterns.
  * Tokens are keyed on the vSphere MoRef where available, so they survive a
    rename.

Runs as you -- no service account, no sudo, no root install. It is an
anonymisation tool, not a privilege boundary: an agent that deliberately worked
around it could reach vCenter itself. What it does guarantee is that the normal
path never puts a real identifier in front of the model.

Credentials are read from a file (default ~/.config/govc-safe/creds, mode 0600)
rather than the environment, so they are not inherited by the agent's shell and
do not show up in `env`. They are never printed and never passed on a command
line.
"""

